@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Split-screen co-op
+
+Two players on one console: Player 1 is the Link the game always has, Player 2 a second Link on
+controller 2. Each has their own camera and half of the screen (side by side), and either player can
+move the story on. PC-only (`TARGET_PC`); the GameCube code paths are unchanged.
+
+## Turning it on
+
+Options menu (Minus on the Switch, the touch pad on the PS5, F1 or L+R+Z on the Mac) > Graphics >
+**Split-screen co-op**: *Two players*. Player 2 joins the next time Player 1 is free to move (not in
+a cutscene or a menu), next to Player 1, and leaves when it is turned off. On the PS5, controller 2 is
+the second signed-in user (a guest is fine). The setting is `COS_SPLITSCREEN=1` in `settings.ini` or
+the environment.
+
+Split-screen turns 60 fps interpolation off (it follows one camera); the game runs at its own 30.
+
+## Colours
+
+Graphics > **Player 1's tunic** / **Player 2's tunic**: a colour for each player's clothes (the
+hero's tunic and cap, or the shirt Link wears on Outset at the start): the game's own, red, blue,
+purple, gold, orange, pink, black, white or green. Player 1 keeps the game's own colours by default,
+Player 2 is red, so the two are told apart from the start. Only the clothes change: face, hair,
+belt and boots keep the game's colours (`native/src/pc/game_hooks/pc_splitscreen_tunic.cpp`).
+
+## How the two players share one game
+
+- **The lead.** The world follows one player at a time, the *lead*: the NPCs, events, doors, rooms,
+  music and menus see the lead's Link as "the player", and cutscenes are shown full screen through the
+  lead's camera. Player 1 leads when a scene starts. Whoever talks to someone, opens a door or a
+  chest, gets an item or presses Start becomes the lead, so either player can move the story on.
+- **Cutscenes.** While the lead is in a cutscene, a talk or a menu, the other player waits (hidden)
+  and the screen shows the lead alone; the split comes back when it ends.
+- **Stages.** Only the lead changes the stage (doors to other places, exits, warps, void-outs): if the
+  other player walks into an exit, Player 2 is brought back next to Player 1, or Player 1 is moved
+  next to Player 2. Player 2 is created again in every new stage, next to Player 1.
+- **Staying together.** A player who gets too far from the lead (about 2000 units on foot, 8000 when
+  sailing) or into another room is brought back the same way.
+- **Boats.** When Player 1's boat (the King of Red Lions) is out, Player 2 gets a boat of their own
+  beside it, which they board and sail like Player 1. Only Player 1's boat talks.
+- **Hearts.** The players share the hearts, rupees, items and magic of the save. Only Player 1's hits
+  cost hearts; Player 2 is knocked back but loses none.
+- **Items.** Either player picks up rupees, hearts and items. The restart point is the lead's.
+- **Lock-on.** Each player has their own lock-on (Z targeting); the Links are not each other's
+  targets.
+
+## Limits
+
+- One HUD over both halves: the hearts and the item buttons are the shared save's; the button
+  prompts (A, R) are the lead's.
+- The baton (Wind Waker songs), the telescope and the Picto Box overlay are whole-screen effects
+  of one player at a time.
+- Each Link's blinking and burn/curse effects are shared (cosmetic).
+- The sea's waves and the islands load around the lead.
+
+## Implementation map
+
+- `native/include/pc/pc_splitscreen_ctx.h`: the player context. Index 0 of the per-player tables
+  (player, camera, pad) means the player whose code runs; 0 and 1 swap for Player 2.
+- `native/include/pc/pc_splitscreen.h`, `native/src/pc/game_hooks/pc_splitscreen.cpp`: Player 2's
+  Link, camera and boat, ownership of processes, the lead, the leash, the setting.
+- `game/include/d/d_com_inf_game.h`: a second slot in the window, camera, player and player-status
+  tables, Player 2's Link and boat pointers and lock-on; accessors go through the context.
+- `game/src/f_pc/f_pc_method.cpp`, `f_pc_draw.cpp`, `f_pc_base.cpp`: each process runs in its
+  player's context; what a player's process creates is that player's.
+- `game/src/m_Do/m_Do_graphic.cpp`: the painter draws each half through its camera, copies it out
+  and puts the two side by side; the second half re-enters the 3D scene into the draw lists
+  (`pc_ss_redraw_scene_for_window`) without advancing animations, particles or paint-time effects.
+- `game/src/d/d_camera.cpp`: Player 2's camera (the game's unused second camera profile); only the
+  camera being drawn sets the view, only the lead's is the sound listener.
+- `game/src/d/actor/d_a_player_main.cpp`: per-Link state that was file-static, the model data both
+  Links share, Player 2's start (no opening cutscene, restart point or boat start).
+- `game/src/d/d_event.cpp`, `d_event_manager.cpp`, `d_demo.cpp`, `d_stage.cpp`,
+  `d_com_inf_game.cpp`: the lead rules for events, cutscene casting and stage changes.
+- `game/src/d/actor/d_a_ship.cpp`, `d_a_grid.cpp`, `game/src/f_op/f_op_actor_mng.cpp`: Player 2's
+  boat and its sail.
